          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "repercussão is a learned borrowing from Latin repercussiō \"a rebounding, a reflection\" (EtymDB, Lewis & Short), from repercutere \"to strike back\", built on quatere \"to shake, to strike\"."
            }
          ]
        },
